# Cost vs Revenue Model

An interactive HTML chart lives at `docs/cost-vs-revenue.html`. It models trefolio's monthly revenue, cost, and profit as customers scale across Free / Bifolio / Trefolio tiers.

## Opening It

The file needs an HTTP server (no `file://` URLs in the browser tool). Start one and open:

```bash
cd docs && python3 -m http.server 8847 &
open http://localhost:8847/cost-vs-revenue.html
```

If port 8847 is busy, pick another (8848, 8850, etc.).

## What It Contains

- **Sliders**: Total customers (0–5K) and tier distribution (% Free / Bifolio / Trefolio)
- **Chart**: Revenue (green), Cost (red), Net Profit (blue dashed), breakeven line (amber)
- **Metrics**: MRR, total cost, breakeven point, profit margin
- **Breakdown cards**: Per-tier user count, revenue, variable cost, and current Alpha Vantage plan
- **Alpha Vantage tiered pricing**: Automatically steps through real AV plans ($49.99–$249.99/mo) based on Trefolio user count

## Updating the Model

Key constants are in the `<script>` block:

- `BIFOLIO_NET` / `TREFOLIO_NET` — net revenue per user after Stripe fees
- `VAR_BIFOLIO` / `VAR_TREFOLIO` — per-user variable costs (SnapTrade, OpenAI)
- `AV_TIERS` — Alpha Vantage plan tiers with `maxUsers`, `cost`, `plan`, `reqMin`
- `infraCost()` — infrastructure cost tiers based on total user count

When pricing, API costs, or infrastructure costs change, update these constants and the assumptions text at the bottom of the page.
